schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Capacity building is the highest-return investment a node can make"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Capacity building is slow but essential. Invest in your members'
    skills, it's the highest-return investment your node can make."
  evidence: >-
    Stated directly as the article's closing assertion in "Moving Forward";
    no study, comparison, or named case is cited to support the
    "highest-return" framing.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/building-internal-capacity.md
  interpretation: >-
    Functions as the article's rhetorical closing argument for prioritizing
    member skill-building over other node investments (e.g. paying external
    consultants).
  uncertainty: >-
    An unevidenced, opinionated claim — the article has no References
    section and no data comparing capacity-building investment against
    alternative uses of node time/resources. Treat as practitioner belief,
    not a measured finding.
